+Concise Bounded Description
+---------------------------
+
+To extract just the information about one resource from a larger graph, use
+:meth:`~rdflib.graph.Graph.cbd`. It returns a new graph containing the
+*Concise Bounded Description* of the resource, as defined in the W3C Member
+Submission `CBD <https://www.w3.org/Submission/CBD/>`_:
+
+* all triples whose subject is the resource;
+* the descriptions of any blank nodes reached as objects, followed
+  recursively;
+* the reification statements (``rdf:Statement``) whose ``rdf:subject`` or
+  ``rdf:object`` is the resource, along with their own descriptions.
+
+Triples where the resource is only the object, and the descriptions of named
+(non-blank) nodes, are not included::
+
+   >>> from rdflib import Graph, URIRef, BNode, Literal
+   >>> from rdflib.namespace import FOAF
+   >>> g = Graph()
+   >>> bob = URIRef("http://example.org/bob")
+   >>> g.add((bob, FOAF.name, Literal("Bob")))
+   >>> g.add((bob, FOAF.based_near, BNode()))
+   >>> g.add((bob, FOAF.knows, URIRef("http://example.org/alice")))
+   >>> len(g.cbd(bob))
+   3
+
